hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"890","On the authority of Hazrat Uqbah bin Aamir, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The best right to dowry is that which is very easy and easy (to pay).\""
"891","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that Umrah bint Jaun sought refuge in Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) when she was sent to him (in a secluded place) i.e. when he married her. So the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"You have indeed sought the refuge of the one who gives refuge.\" Then he divorced her and ordered Hazrat Usamah, may Allah be pleased with him, to give him three clothes as a reward. (It was narrated by Ibn Majah and it is an abandoned narrator in its chain of transmission. Its original story was narrated in Sahih Bukhari by Hazrat Abu Sayyid Sa’idi, may God be pleased with him.)"
"892","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik that the Prophet saw a yellow mark on the clothes of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, so he said: \"What is this?\" He said: Messenger of Allah! I have married a woman for gold equivalent to a palm kernel. He said: \"May Allah bless you, do the Walima, even if it is a goat.\" (Bukhari and Muslim. And the words are Muslim's)."
"893","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When one of you is invited to the feast of Walima, he should arrive there.\""
"894","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The worst food is the food of the feast in which the one who comes (with pleasure) is forbidden and the one who refuses to come is invited.\" And whoever does not accept Dawat Walima, he has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"895","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When one of you is invited (for a meal), he should accept it.\" If it is due to fasting, then he should pray (for the inviter), and if it is not due to fasting, then he should eat.” (Also narrated by Muslim.) And there is a similar narration in Muslim from Hazrat Jabir (RA) and in it he said: “If he wishes, then he should eat and if he wishes, he should leave it.”"
"896","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Eating Walimah on the first day is right, and eating on the second day is customary, and eating on the third day is fame and hypocrisy.\" And whoever commits hypocrisy, Allah will disgrace him.”"
"897","On the authority of Hazrat Safiyyah bint Sheebah, she says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Walimah for one of his wives with two mudjus. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"898","On the authority of Hazrat Anas, he says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed between Khaibar and Madinah for three days. A tent was set up there for the sake of Hazrat Safiyyah (to spend the night of marriage with her), so I invited the Muslims to the feast of the Prophet (peace be upon him). There was no bread or meat in it. The only thing in this (ceremony) was that you ordered the leather table to be laid, and dates, cheese and ghee were placed on it. (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)."
"899","It was narrated from one of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: When two men have given a feast, accept the invitation of the one whose door is closer, and if one of them has taken the initiative, then accept the invitation of the one who took the initiative."
"900","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Juhaifa, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"I do not eat while leaning.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"901","On the authority of Hazrat Umar bin Abu Salama, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \"O child! In the name of Allah, recite \"Eat with your right hand and eat in front of you.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"902","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a large bowl full of thareed was presented in the service of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: \"Eat from the sides of the bowl, and do not eat from the middle of it, because the blessing comes from the middle of it.\""
"903","Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Do not eat with your left hand,” because Satan eats with his left hand.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"904","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Qutada, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When one of you drinks, he should not breathe in the vessel.” (Bukhari and Muslim) A similar narration from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, is also in Abu Dawud, and this addition is added: “Do not blow into it.”"
"905","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to divide his share between his wives who are pure and used to act justly in this matter, and he used to say: “O Allah! According to what is in my power, it is my distribution, and what is not in my power, but in your power, do not blame me for it.”"
"906","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “A person who has two wives and his inclination is towards one, he will be in such a state on the Day of Resurrection that one side of him will be paralyzed.”"
"907","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Anas, he says that the Masnoon method is that if a person marries a virgin in the presence of her husband, he should stay with her (the new bride) for seven days, and then divide the share. And when the husband marries the widow in the presence of the virgin, he should stay with her for three days, then divide the turn. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are Bukhari's)."
"908","It was narrated from Hazrat Umm Salamah that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, he stayed with her for three days and said: \"You are not worthless (and despised) in the presence of your family.\" If you want, I will fix seven days for you. And if I set seven days for you, I will also spend seven days with all my other women.” (Muslim)"
"909","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that Hazrat Saudah bint Zamaa gave the day of her turn to Hazrat Aisha, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to divide his day and Hazrat Saudah's day for Hazrat Aisha. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"910","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Urwa, may God have mercy on him, who says that Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: O nephew! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give priority to any of us over others in the division of staying with us. And there is hardly a day in which you do not come to us all. You used to go to each wife but did not have intercourse until you reached the wife whose turn it was during the day, so you used to spend the night with her. (It was narrated by Ahmad and Abu Dawud. And these words are Abu Dawud’s, and Hakim called it Sahih.) And it is narrated in Muslim on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said that when the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, would perform the Asr prayer, he would go round to all his wives, and then he would also be close to them...Al-Hadith."
"911","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, used to inquire: \"Where will I be tomorrow?\" (To whom is my turn tomorrow?'') His intention was the day of Hazrat Aisha (RA), so his wives allowed him to stay wherever he wanted. Then he stayed with Hazrat Aisha (RA). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"912","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha, she says that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, intended to travel, he would cast lots among his wives, so the wife whose name was drawn would take her with him. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"913","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Zam'ah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"None of you should beat his wife like a slave.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"914","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the wife of Hazrat Thabit bin Qays, may Allah be pleased with him, came to the service of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I do not find any fault in the morals and religion of Thabit bin Qays, but I find disobedience and ingratitude to be abhorrent in the presence of Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Will you return his garden to him?\" He said: \"Yes!\" So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"(O Thabit!) Take your garden and divorce her.\" (Narrated by Bukhari, and in a tradition of Bukhari, he ordered her to divorce. It is in Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi, and Imam Tirmidhi has described it as good.) That the wife of Hazrat Thabit bin Qays, may God be pleased with him, divorced her, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fixed the period of one period for her. And Ibn In a hadith narrated by Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of Abiyyah on Jeddah: Thabit bin Qays was not beautiful and his wife said: If I had not been afraid of Allah, I would have spat on his face when he came to me (in private)."
"915","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Divorce is the most evil thing in the sight of Allah, the Most High, among the lawful things.\""
"916","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that he divorced his wife during the period of the Prophet while she was menstruating. So Hazrat Umar asked the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about this. He said: Tell him to turn back and stop it until Tahar begins. And this is the iddat (time) which Allah has ordered that women should be divorced.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in the tradition of Muslim: \"Tell her to turn to him, then divorce her in such a state that she is in a state of purity or pregnant.\" And in a hadith of Muslim, Ibn Umar (RA) said (to the one who inquired about divorcing a woman during menstruation): If you divorce a woman once or twice, then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to return to her, then keep her with me until the second menstruation, then give her a period of time until Tahar, and then divorce her before laying hands on her. two And if you divorce her three times, then you have disobeyed the command of your Lord to divorce your wife. And there is another hadith: Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) returned that woman to me and did not count this divorce as anything and said: \"When a woman becomes pure from menstruation, divorce her or stop her.\""
"917","There is a hadith on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that during the reign of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, and until the first two years of the caliphate of Hazrat Umar, three talaqs were counted as one talaq. Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \"The people have begun to hasten in a matter in which there was a respite for them.\" (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"918","On the authority of Hazrat Mahmud bin Labaid, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed about a man who had divorced his wife three times, so he stood up in anger and said: \"Is the Book of Allah being played with while I am still among you?\" A man stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! Should I not kill him? (Narrated by Nasa'i and its narrator is Saqa)."
"919","On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that Abu Raqana divorced Umm Raqana, then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him: \"Go back to your wife.\" Abu Raqana said: I have divorced her three times. He said: I know. You turn to him.'' Ruqana (RA) divorced his wife Suhaima and then said: By Allah! I had intended a divorce. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) returned his wife to him."
"920","Hadhrat Abu Huraira, may God be pleased with him, says that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There are three things that are true to be done intentionally, and to say them jokingly is also true: marriage, divorce, and return.\" It is mentioned in the Qur'an: \"It is not permissible to joke about three things: divorce, marriage and freedom.\" Whoever says these matters (even in jest), they will become wajib."
"921","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah has spared my Ummah from the whisperings of their hearts.\" (And this is until) until they act (on these whispers) or say with the tongue.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"922","Narrated by Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Allah has forgiven my ummah for the sins they were forced to commit.\""
"923","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that when a husband declares his wife haram, it is nothing. And he said: Indeed, the best example for you is in the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Narrated by Al-Bukhari.) And in Muslim: When a man declares his wife haram on him, it will count as an oath. He will have to pay for it."
"924","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that when the daughter of Jaun was sent to the private place of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she became close to him, she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: \"You have sought the refuge of the Most High\", so go to your family.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"925","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Jabir, who says that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Divorce can be done only after marriage.\" And freedom is possible only after ownership.”"
"926","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father and he from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is not valid to make a vow for something that a person does not own, nor is it valid for a man to free a slave that he does not own, nor is it valid for him to divorce a woman who is not owned by him.\" This is the most correct of all hadiths.)"
"927","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The pen is lifted from three people: from a sleeping person until he wakes up, from a child until he becomes an adult. And from a madman until he becomes sane or becomes sane.”"
"928","It is narrated about Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (RA) that he was asked about a man who divorces, then withdraws and does not make him a witness. So he said: Appoint a witness when divorcing a woman and approaching her. (Abu Dawud narrated it in the same manner and its chain of transmission is authentic.) Imam Bayhaqi mentioned this tradition with these words: Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (RA) was asked about a person who approaches his wife but does not produce a witness. He should make a witness now. Al-Tabarani has added these words in a hadith: He should seek forgiveness from Allah."
"929","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that when he divorced his wife, the Prophet (PBUH) said to Hazrat Umar (RA): \"Tell him to go back to his wife.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"930","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced his wives and made (halal) haram, then he made this haram haram and made expiation. (Narrated by Tirmidhi and its narrator is Thaqa)."
"931","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that when four months have passed, the one who commits adultery will be made to stand (in front of the ruler of time) until he divorces. And the divorce will not take place until he gives the divorce. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"932","It was narrated from Hazrat Sulaiman bin Yasar, may God have mercy on him, that I found more than ten companions of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, who used to stand up (in court) and ask the person who did evil. (Narrated by Shafi'i.)"
"933","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas that the Illah year of Jahiliyyah lasted for two years. Allah Almighty fixed its period of four months, so if the period is less than four months, it will not be counted. (Narrated by Bayhaqi)."
"934","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man appeared to his wife and then had sexual intercourse with her. Later, he came to the Prophet's service and said that I had intercourse with my wife before paying the expiation. He said: \"Now do not go to him until you fulfill the commandment of Allah Ta'ala.\""
"935","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Salama bin Sakhr, may Allah be pleased with him, who says that when Ramadan began, I feared that I would have intercourse with my wife. One (moonlit) night, a part of his body was exposed in front of me, so I sat with him. So the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \"Free the slave.\" I said: I am not the owner of anyone except my neck. He said: \"Then fast for two consecutive months.\" I said: I have suffered from this problem because of fasting. He said: \"Good! Then feed a basket of dates to sixty poor people."
"936","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that such and such a person asked: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me, if one of us finds his wife in a bad state, what should he do? If he narrates it to others, it is a very shameful act, and if he remains silent, it is also a very difficult act. You didn't answer it. Then when he came later, he said, \"Research what I have asked you, I myself have suffered from it.\" So Allah revealed the verses of Surah Noor. You read those verses in front of him and advised him and reminded him of the punishment of Allah and warned him that the punishment of this world is much lighter than the punishment of the Hereafter. He said: No, by the One who has sent you with the truth! I have not blamed him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called this woman and advised her in the same way. He also said: No, by the one who has sent you with the truth! Of course this is false. Then you started with this man. He took four oaths by Allah, then he also took oaths from the woman, then differentiated between the two. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"937","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the two cursers: \"You two are accountable to Allah.\" One of the two is a liar. Now you have no right over this woman.\" He (the man) said: O Messenger of Allah! My wealth (give it to me.) He said: \"If you have spoken the truth about him, then that wealth is in return for what you have made lawful for yourself in his private place.\" And if you have accused him, it is even more remote for you to get this wealth.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"938","Narrated by Hazrat Anas, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Look at the woman. If she gives birth to a white child with straight hair, then it is her husband's.\" And if she gives birth to a child whose eyes are gray and whose hair is curly, then that child will be hers about whom the husband has slandered her.” (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"939","It was narrated from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a person to place his hand over the mouth of the person taking an oath during the fifth oath, and he said: \"This (fifth oath) is obligatory.\""
"940","It is narrated from Hazrat Sahl bin Saad, may Allah be pleased with him, in the story of the two cursing people, he says that when they both finished cursing, the man said: O Messenger of Allah! If I keep her now, it will be as if I have falsely accused her.' So (saying this) he gave her three divorces before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"941","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, a man came to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said: (O Messenger of Allah!) My wife does not reject the hand of anyone who touches her. He said: \"Take him away.\" He said: I am afraid that my soul will be behind him. He said: \"Then continue to take advantage of it.\" (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Bazar, and its narrators are trustworthy.) And Imam al-Nasa'i narrated it in another chain of narration on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, with the words that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Divorce him.\" He said, \"I cannot endure without him.\" He said: \"Then keep him with you.\""
"942","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) that when the verse about the two cursers was revealed, he heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: “A woman who marries a child in a nation who is not from that nation, then that woman has nothing to do with Allah Ta’ala (Mercy and Religion). And Allah Ta'ala will never admit such a woman to His Paradise. And the man who disowns his child while he is looking at it, then (on the Day of Resurrection) Allah will be veiled from him and will humiliate him in front of all the first and last creation."
"943","It is narrated from Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that whoever confesses his child even for a moment, he has no right to deny it. (It was narrated by Bayhaqi and this tradition is Hasan Muqoof.)"
"944","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that a person said: O Messenger of Allah! My wife has given birth to a black child. You asked him: \"Do you have any camels?\" He said: Yes. He inquired: \"What are their colors?\" He said: Red. He inquired: \"Is there anyone among them who is grey?\" He said: Yes. He inquired: \"Where did that (colour) come from?\" He said: A vein must have drawn it. So he said: \"Then a vein must have pulled this son of yours too.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) And in a hadith of Muslim, he was referring to the negation of this child. And it is at the end of this tradition that you did not give him permission to reject the child."
"945","It is narrated from Hazrat Masoor Bin Mukharama (RA) that Subiyyah Islamiyah (RA) gave birth to a child a few days after the death of her husband. Later, she attended the Prophet's service and asked permission for marriage. You gave him permission to marry and he got married. (It was narrated by Bukhari and the original of this hadith is in both Bukhari and Muslim.) And in one tradition, she gave birth to a child forty days after the death of her husband. And the words of Muslim tradition are that Zahri said: I don't think there is any harm in a woman marrying in the state of nifas, but her husband does not go near her until he is purified (by bathing in nifas)."
"946","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that Hazrat Barira (RA) was ordered to observe three menstrual periods. (It has been narrated by Ibn Majah and its narrator is Taqqa, but this narration is invalid.)"
"947","Shaabi has narrated from Fatima bint Qays (may God be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of God be upon him) said about the polygamist: “There is no residence for her, nor bread and sustenance.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"948","Narrated by Hazrat Umm Atiya, may Allah be pleased with her: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"No woman should mourn a dead person for more than three days, except for her husband.\" She should mourn him for four months and ten days. (During the period of mourning) she may not wear colored clothes but may wear a striped cloth (of dyed yarn). Do not apply headscarf, or touch perfume, but when she is free from menstruation, she can use a little Oud Hindi or Azfar.\" (Bukhari and Muslim - and these words are Muslim's.) And in Abu Dawood and Nasa'i there is this addition: \"Do not even apply henna and dye.\" And in Nasa'i: \"Do not even comb.\""
"949","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Umm Salama, she says that after the death of Hazrat Abu Salama, I put Alwa on my eyes, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: \"It enhances the beauty of the face.\" So apply it only at night and remove it during the day. And don't comb your hair with something fragrant or with henna (don't wash your head) because it is a dye.\" I said: Then what should I comb with? He said: \"With berry leaves (by boiling them in water).\""
"950","It was narrated from Umm Salamah that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah! My daughter's husband has died and she is suffering from conjunctivitis. Shall we put silver in his eyes? He said: “No.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"951","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir (RA) that he says that my aunt was divorced and wanted to go out (during Idda) with the intention of picking the fruit of her date palm, so a man scolded her for leaving the house. She came to the service of the Prophet, so he said: \"Yes! You can pluck the fruit of your palms. It is quite possible that you may give charity from it or do some other good deed.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"952","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Furiyyah bint Malik that her husband went out in search of his (runaway) slaves, so they killed him. It is narrated by Fariya that I inquired from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, about my return to Makkah, because my husband left me no house in his possession and no alimony. He said: \"Yes! (You can go to your home.\") When I reached the room, he called me and said: \"You stay in your house until your Idda is completed.\" It is narrated by Fariya that then I completed Idda for four months and ten days in this house. She says that then Hazrat Uthman also gave a decision accordingly. (It has been narrated by Ahmad and the four. Tirmidhi, Dahli, Ibn Hibban and Hakim etc. have declared it to be Sahih.)"
"953","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Fatima bint Qays, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! My husband has given me three divorces and I am afraid that no one will forcibly enter my place. Narrator states that when you ordered her, she moved from there. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"954","It was narrated from Hazrat Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Sunnah of our Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, should not be confused with us. When the husband of the mother's son dies, her Idda is four months and ten days."
"955","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that reading means purity. (It has been narrated by Imam Malik under a Qasa with a valid chain of transmission.)"
"956","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the divorce of a slave girl is two divorces and her period is two periods. (It has been narrated by Darqutani and he has also narrated it as Marfu’, but he has called it weak. Also, this tradition has been narrated by Imam Abu Dawood, Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah with reference to Hazrat Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her. And Hakim has called it Sahih, but other muhadditheen have contradicted him. They agree that it is weak.)"
"957","On the authority of Hazrat Ruifa bin Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is not lawful for a person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to irrigate the crops of others with his own water.\""
"958","It was narrated from Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) about the wife of the missing man that she would wait for four years and then perform the Eid for four months and ten days. (Narrated by Malik and Shafi'i, may God have mercy on him.)"
"959","It was narrated from Hazrat Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The wife of a missing person remains his wife until she (the wife) receives clear information.”"
"960","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one should spend the night with a woman unless that man is her husband or a mahram.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"961","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one should be alone with a woman unless he has a mahram with her.” (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"962","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) said about the captive women of Autas: “One should not have sexual intercourse with a pregnant woman until her child is born, and one should not have sexual intercourse with a non-pregnant woman until she has had one period.”"
"963","Narrated by Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The child belongs to the owner of the bed and is a stone for the adulterer.\""
"964","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Sucking (the breast) once or twice does not prove haram.\" (Muslim)"
"965","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Consider who your brothers are. Because feeding is valid only if it is due to hunger.” (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"966","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha that Sahlah bint Suhail came and said: O Messenger of Allah! Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, lives with us in our house, he has grown up like men. He said: \"Give him your milk. You will become forbidden to him.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"967","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that Abul Qais's brother Aflah sought permission to come to Hazrat Aisha after hijab. Hazrat Aisha narrates that I refused to give him permission. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, I informed him of what I had done with him. He ordered me to allow him to come to me and said: \"He is your uncle.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"968","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the order that was revealed in the Qur'an was the ten certain rations that proved sanctity. Therefore, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died, he was recited in the Qur'an. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"969","It is narrated from Ibn Abbas (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) was persuaded to marry the daughter of Hamza (RA) and he said: \"She is not lawful for me\" because she is the daughter of my foster brother. And what is forbidden because of lineage is also forbidden because of adoption.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"970","On the authority of Hazrat Umm Salama, may Allah be pleased with her, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Only breastfeeding that opens the bowels and precedes the period of weaning is considered sacred.”"
"971","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Only breastfeeding during two years is valid. (It has been narrated by Darqutni and Ibn Udi in Marfu' and Muquf, and both have preferred Muquf)."
"972","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Breastfeeding is that which strengthens the bones and produces meat.” (Narrated by Abu Dawood.)"
"973","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Uqbah bin Harith (RA) that he married Umm Yahya bint Abu Ahab (RA) and a woman came and said, \"I have breastfed you both.\" Hazrat Uqbah (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) and he said: \"How (can you keep her in your marriage?) when the adoption has been notified.\" So Hazrat Uqbah (RA) divorced this woman and she married someone else. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"974","On the authority of Ziyad Sahmi, he states that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a foolish woman to breastfeed. (It is narrated by Abu Dawud and it is a messenger because Ziyad did not have the privilege of being a companion.)"
"975","On the authority of Hazrat Aisha, she said that Hind bint Utbah, the wife of Abu Sufyan, came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! Abu Sufyan is a stingy and greedy man. He does not spend enough for me and my children, except that I take some of his wealth without telling him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"In a good way, you can take as much of his wealth as is sufficient for you and your children.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"976","Narrated by Hazrat Tariq Moharebi, may Allah be pleased with him, he says that when we came to Madinah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was addressing the people standing on the pulpit. He used to say: \"The hand of the giver is high and high.\" And you start with those for whom you are a sponsor, that is, your mother, your father, your sister and your brother, and then those who are closest to you in order of rank.”"
"977","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is (obligatory on the owner) to provide food, drink and clothing for the slave.\" And he should only be assigned to that task for which he has the power.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"978","Hazrat Hakeem bin Muawiya Qashiri narrates on the authority of his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! What right does his wife have over any of us? He said: \"(That right) is that when you eat yourself, feed him also.\" When you wear it yourself, wear it too and do not hit him on the face and do not speak ill of him."
"979","Hazrat Jabir (RA) narrates from the Prophet (PBUH) in a long hadith about Hajj that he said about women: \"It is obligatory on you to provide for their bread and sustenance and their clothing according to the law.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"980","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"It is sufficient for a man to be guilty of wasting the sustenance and expenses of whom he is responsible and responsible.\""
"981","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) about a pregnant woman whose husband has died that there is no maintenance for her. (It was narrated by Bayhaqi and its narrator is reliable, but Imam Bayhaqi said that it is safe to suspend it. The negation of alimony is proven by the hadith of Fatima bint Qays (may God be pleased with her) which was passed down (under 947). It was narrated by Muslim.)"
"982","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The upper hand is better than the lower hand.\" Let each of you start (expenditure) from those whom he supports. Lest the wife should say, \"Give me alimony or give me a divorce.\""
"983","It was narrated from Hazrat Saeed bin Musayb, may God have mercy on him, that a man who has nothing to provide for his wife will be separated. (This hadith has been narrated by Saeed bin Mansur from Sufyan and he has narrated from Abu Zanad that I asked Saeed bin Musayb: Is this a Sunnah? He replied that yes it is a Sunnah. And this hadith is authoritative.)"
"984","It has been narrated about Hazrat Umar that he wrote to the commanders of the army about such men who were absent from their wives (due to being in the army) that they should send maintenance to their wives or divorce them. If they divorce, send the alimony for the period they have withheld. (It was narrated by Imam Shafi’i and Bayhaqi with a hasan chain of transmission.)"
"985","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) that a man came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH) and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have one dinar. He said: \"Spend it on yourself.\" He said: I have another. He said: \"Spend it on your children.\" He then said: I have another one. He said: \"Spend it on your wife.\" He said: I have another one. He said: \"Spend it on your servant.\" He said: I have another one. He said: \"You know better (where it should be spent.\") (Shafi'i and Abu Dawood have narrated it and these words are Abu Dawood's. And Nasa'i and Hakim also narrated it. In their tradition, the wife is mentioned before the children.)"
"986","Bahz bin Hakim narrates from his father (Hakim) and he (Bahz) from his grandfather (Muawiyah Qashiri) that I said: O Messenger of Allah! To whom should I treat and be kind? He said: \"From my mother.\" I then asked: Then from whom? He said: \"From my mother.\" I then asked: Then from whom? He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then said: \"From my mother.\" I again asked: \"Then from whom?\" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"From his father. Then from the relatives by rank.\""
"987","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah! This is my bare liver, my stomach was a vessel for him, my breast was a mask for him and my embrace was a shelter for him. Her father has divorced me and wants to take this child away from me. He said: \"As long as you do not marry (second) then you are more entitled to it.\""
"988","It was narrated from Abu Huraira that a woman said: O Messenger of Allah! My husband wants to take away my child from me, even though he (the child) benefits me and brings me water from the well of Abu Anba. Meanwhile, her husband also arrived. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O child! This is your father and this is your mother. Take the hand of whoever you want from the two of them.'' (It is narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu and Tirmidhi says it is Sahih.)"
"989","It is narrated from Hazrat Rafi bin Sinan that he himself became a Muslim and his wife refused to accept Islam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the mother sit on one side and the father on the other side and placed the child between them. Give guidance to this child.\" So the child leaned towards the father and the father caught him. (Narrated by Abu Dawud and Nasa'i and Al-Hakim called it Sahih.)"
"990","It is narrated from Hazrat Bara bin Azib (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) decided the daughter of Hazrat Hamza (RA) in favor of her aunt and said: \"The aunt is equal to the mother.\" It was narrated by Bukhari. And Ahmad has narrated it from the hadith of Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he (peace be upon him) said: \"The girl will stay with her aunt because the aunt is the mother.\""
"991","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When a servant comes to one of you with food, if he does not make that servant sit with him (to eat), then he must give him one or two morsels.\" (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are from Bukhari)."
"992","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A woman was punished because of a cat.\" He imprisoned the cat (for so long) that it died. So the woman went to hell because of that cat. She (the woman) did not feed the cat, but kept it tied up and did not let it go free, so that it would eat the insects of the earth, etc.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"993","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Mas'ud, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \"A Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I (Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him) am the Messenger of Allah, then it is not permissible and permissible to kill him except in three cases: a married adulterer, a life for a life, and a person who abandons his religion and separates from the community (of Muslims).\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"994","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “It is not permissible to kill a Muslim man except in one of three cases: A married adulterer.” He will be stoned to death. (Second) A man who intentionally kills a Muslim will be killed. And (third) the man who leaves the circle of Islam and starts fighting against Allah and His Messenger, he will be killed or executed or exiled."
"995","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The first cases that will be decided between people on the Day of Resurrection will be cases of blood.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"996","Hazrat Samura (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever kills his slave, we will kill him. And whoever cuts off any part of him, we will cut off that part of him.\" (It was narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu and Tirmidhi called it Hasan. This is a tradition of Hasan Basri from Samra and there is a difference in the hearing of Hasan Basri from Samra.) In the tradition of Abu Dawud and Nasa'i: \"Whoever castrates his slave, We will castrate him.\""
"997","On the authority of Hazrat Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"The son will not be retaliated against the father.\" (It was narrated by Ahmad, Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah, Ibn Jarood and Bayhaqi declared it authentic, and Tirmidhi said that there is confusion in this hadith.)"
"998","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Juhaifa (RA) that I asked Hazrat Ali (RA): Do you people have anything other than the Qur'an revealed through revelation? He replied: No, by the One who grew the seed and created the soul! Except for the understanding that Allah gives to a person about the Qur'an and what is written in this scripture. I asked what is in this scripture? He said that the commandments of Dayt are the command to set a prisoner free and that no Muslim shall be killed in exchange for a disbeliever. And even the lowest of them can give Aman on their behalf. And they are a handful compared to the foreigners. And a believer will not be killed in exchange for an unbeliever, nor can a covenant (dhimmi) be killed during his covenant period."
"999","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik that a slave girl was found in such a condition that her head was placed between two stones and crushed. People asked him who has done this to you? So and so? So and so? Even when he mentioned a Jew, he nodded: (Yes.) So the Jew was arrested, then he confessed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his head to be crushed between two stones. (Bukhari and Muslim. These words are from Muslim.)"
"1000","It was narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him) that a boy from the poor people cut off the ear of a boy from the rich people, so these (rich) people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). You have not ordained anything for them. (Narrated by Ahmad and all three with a Sahih chain of transmission.)"
"1001","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib narrated from his father and he narrated from his grandfather that a man pierced the knee of another with a horn. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Make me pay him. He said: \"(No!) even if you are healed.\" He then came to you and said: Give me retribution. You made him retaliate. After that he came to you again and said: O Messenger of Allah! I'm lame. He said: \"I forbade you but you disobeyed me.\" May Allah remove you and your lameness is nullified.” Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade taking revenge for the injury before the injured person is healed. (This hadith has been narrated by Ahmad and Darqutni and is called Maaloool due to its transmission.)"
"1002","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira (RA) that two women of the Huzail tribe fought with each other, and one of them hit the other with a stone and killed the woman and what was in her womb. So those people brought a dispute to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, decided that the birth of the fetus is Ghara, meaning a slave or a concubine. And declared the death of the (murderer) woman (by) her heirs. And the heirs of this (deity) were made the children of the deceased and other heirs along with them. Hamal bin Nabagha Hazli said: O Messenger of Allah! How can we pay for such a child who neither drank nor ate nor spoke nor screamed? That will be in vain. He said: \"Because of this rhyming word, which he said, he seems to be among the brothers of the priests.\" (Bukhari and Muslim). Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Hamal bin Nabagha stood up and narrated that I was between two women and one of them killed the other. (He narrated it briefly and Ibn Hibban and Hakim called it Sahih.)"
"1003","It was narrated from Hazrat Anas that his paternal grandmother Rubai'a bint Nazr broke the front tooth of a girl. Rubai'a's relatives asked him for forgiveness, but the girls refused. Then he offered to give a dowry, but he rejected that too. So he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and refused to accept anything except Qisas. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered retribution. Hearing this, Hazrat Anas bin Nazr said: O Messenger of Allah! Will Rabi'a's tooth be broken? No, by the Most Holy One who has given you the truth and sent you! His tooth will not be broken. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Anas! Allah's decision is retribution.'' Then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There are some servants of Allah who, if they swear by Allah, Allah fulfills their oath.\" (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are Bukhari's)."
"1004","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A person who is killed in a riot (so that his killer is not known) or is killed with a stone, whip or stick in such a way that the killer is not aware, then his death will be the death of murder.\" And the person who will be killed intentionally is retribution. The curse of Allah is upon the person who prevents him from taking revenge.”"
"1005","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Umar, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When a man captures a man and another kills the captured man, the murderer will be killed and the capturer will be imprisoned.\""
"1006","It was narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Belmani that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed a Muslim in exchange for a covenant (dhimmi) and said: \"I am closer to the person who fulfills his covenant.\""
"1007","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that a slave was killed by deception, then Hazrat Umar said: If all the people of Sana'a had participated in his killing, I would have killed them all in return. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1008","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Shureeh al-Khuza'i, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"After this sermon of mine, if a man is killed, his heirs have two options: either take the death or kill the murderer in exchange for the slain.\""
"1009","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm narrates from his father (Muhammad) and he (Abu Bakr) from his grandfather (Amr bin Hazm) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) wrote to the people of Yemen. Then narrated a long hadith. There is also this in it: \"Whoever kills an innocent Muslim and there is proof of this murder, Qisas is obligatory upon him\" unless the heirs of the deceased agree (to the deed). And the death of one soul is a hundred camels. And in the nose there is also full deity, if it is cut off from the root. And for the two eyes, the tongue, and the two lips, there is full deity. (Similarly) there is full deity in the organ specific. And the two testicles have a full diet. And in the back there is a whole day. And one foot has half a day. And a third is in the deep wound of the brain and stomach. And a wound that breaks a bone and dislodges it is worth fifteen camels. And there are ten camels in each finger and toe. And the value of one tooth is five camels. And in such a wound from which the bones are visible, five camels are buried. And the man will be killed in exchange for the woman. And those who do not have (camels and) if they have gold, they will be charged a thousand dinars.”"
"1010","Hazrat Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The death penalty for murder will be divided into five parts: twenty rights, twenty tribes, twenty daughters of Makhaz, twenty daughters of Lubun, and twenty Banu Lubun.” And Ibn Abi Shaybah has narrated it in another way, and it is more correct than Marfu'. And Abu Dawud and Tirmidhi have narrated it with authority on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of Abiyyah on the authority of Jeddah: “Thirty rights in Dayt, thirty trunks and forty pregnant camels with babies in their bellies” (will be received.)"
"1011","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: “The people who disobey Allah the Most are of three types: (one) who kills in the Haram of Allah, (second) one who kills his non-slayer, and (third) one who kills because of the enmity of Jahiliyyah.”"
"1012","Hadhrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The death of a wrongful act, i.e., suspicion of intent, which is done with a whip and a stick, is a hundred camels.\" Among them will be forty she-camels with babies in their bellies.” (Narrated by Abu Dawud, Al-Nisa’i and Ibn Majah, and Ibn Hibban said it to be Sahih.)"
"1013","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This and this”, that is, the ring finger and the thumb, are equal. Ten camels in return."
"1014","Hazrat Amr bin Shuaib has narrated from his father and he has narrated from his grandfather (Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The person who treated someone, even though he is not well-known in medicine, then kills someone or harms someone else, he will be held responsible.” This hadith has also been narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim, but the one who has narrated this tradition as a messenger is more powerful than the narrators who have narrated it as received.)"
"1015","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr, the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \"In those wounds in which the flesh is removed from the bone, there are five camels (deat).\" (This has been narrated by Imam Ahmad, may God have mercy on him, and all four others) and Imam Ahmad, may God have mercy on him, has narrated this addition: \"All the fingers are equal,\" that is, their deat is ten ten camels."
"1016","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The diet of the dhimmis is half of the diet of the Muslims.” (Narrated by Ahmad and the four). Khazima declared it to be correct.)"
"1017","It was narrated from him (Abdullah ibn Amr, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The death of a suspected murder is as bad as a murder of intent.\" But the (suspected) murderer will not be killed. That (suspicious intention) is such that Satan jumps (among people) (and incites and incites them to murder) as a result of which blood is spoiled without any enmity or taking up arms."
"1018","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that during the reign of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) a man killed another man, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fixed his death penalty at twelve thousand (dirhams). (Narrated by all four of them. Ornasai and Abu Hatim preferred the transmission of this tradition.)"
"1019","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Ramtha, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I attended the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while my son was with me. He inquired: \"Who is this?\" I said: It is my son. I (openly) say this. He said: \"Indeed, you are not responsible for his crime, nor is he responsible for your crime.\""
"1020","Hazrat Sahl bin Abu Hatmah narrates from some of the elders of his people that Abdullah bin Sahl and Hazrat Muhaissa bin Masoud (RA) left for Khyber because of their poverty. Muhaisa (RA) came to the Jews and said: By Allah! You guys killed him. He said: By Allah! We did not kill him. Then Muhaisa and her brother Huwaysa and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl (may God be pleased with them) all three came (to the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace), and Muhaisa wanted to speak, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Let the elder speak and consider his right.\" \"You meant that the one who is older among you should speak.\" So Hawaisah spoke. Then Muhaisah spoke, and the Messenger of Allah, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \"They will either pay the death of your master and companion or declare war.\" Then he wrote a letter to him in this regard, to which he wrote: By Allah! We did not kill him. Then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Huwaysa, Muhaissa and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, may God be pleased with them: \"Will you swear an oath and be entitled to the blood of your master?\" They said: No. He said: \"Then the Jews swear to you?\" He said that they are not Muslims (therefore their oath is not valid). ) So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him (Abdullah bin Sahl radi Allahu anhu) the diet from his own (Bait al-Mal) and sent a hundred camels to him. Hazrat Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) said that one of them, a red colored camel, kicked me. (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1021","It is narrated from an Ansari Companion that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, maintained the method of Qasamat of the Jahiliyyah. And you accordingly judged a slain among some of the Ansar whom they claimed against the Jews. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1022","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"He who takes up arms against us is not one of us.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1023","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever goes out of obedience (to the Imam) and separates from the Muslim community and dies in that state, then his death will be the death of Jahiliyyah.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1024","It is narrated on the authority of Umm Salamah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Hazrat Ammar (RA) will be killed by a rebel group.” (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1025","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O son of Umm Abd! Do you know what is Allah's decision regarding the rebels of this nation?\" He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"His wounded will not be tortured, nor his captives will be killed, nor will the fugitive be chased, nor will his property be divided as booty.\" It is proven. (Narrated by Ibn Abi Shaiba and al-Hakim.)"
"1026","Hazrat Arfaja bin Shareeh says that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \"Whoever comes to you while you are all united and wants to create division in your congregation, then kill him.\" (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1027","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr.\""
"1028","It was narrated from Imran bin Hussain that Hazrat Yala bin Umayyah had a fight with a person. When one of them bit the other with his teeth, he pulled his hand from his mouth and pulled it out, so that his front tooth broke and fell out. Then both of them took their dispute to the court of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: \"Does one of you bite his brother like a camel?\" There is no religion for him.” (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
"1029","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"If a man peeps into your house without permission and you throw a stone at his eye, then there is no sin on you.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1030","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Bara bin Azib that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided that the protection and supervision of gardens during the day is the responsibility of the owners of the garden. And the protection and supervision of the cattle at night is the responsibility of the cattle owners. And the amount of damage caused by the cattle during the night is on the owners of the cattle. (This hadith has been narrated by all four except Ahmad and Tirmidhi and Ibn Hibban has called it Sahih, but there is a difference in its chain of transmission.)"
"1031","It was narrated from Hazrat Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) about a person who first converted to Islam and then became a Jew, \"I will not sit until he is killed.\" This is the decision of Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him). Then ordered to kill him and he was killed. (Bukhari and Muslim) and in a hadith of Abu Dawud: He was asked to repent before the killing."
"1032","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Kill him who changes his religion.\" (Narrated by Bukhari)."
"1033","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that a blind man had a concubine who used to abuse and speak ill of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace. Those blind companions used to forbid her, but she would not stop. One night, they took a hoe and put it on his stomach and pressed it with their load and killed him. This matter reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: “Beware! You be the witness! His blood went in vain and in vain."
"1034","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira and Hazrat Zaid bin Khalid Jahni that a villager came to the service of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of Allah! I swear to you by Allah that you judge me according to the Book of Allah. And the other one who was wiser than him also said yes! You decide between us according to the Book of Allah and allow me to submit something. He said: \"Explain.\" He said: My son used to work as a laborer for him. He committed adultery with his wife and I was informed that the punishment of stoning was necessary for my son. After that, I inquired from the scholars and they told me that my son's punishment is 100 lashes and one year's exile and his wife's punishment is imprisonment. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul!\" I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah. The slave girls and the goats will be returned to you and your son will be punished with a hundred lashes and exile for a year. And oh nineteen! Go to this man's wife, and if she confesses (to adultery), stone her to death.\" (Bukhari and Muslim and these words are from Muslim)."
"1035","On the authority of Hazrat Ubada bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Get (the rules of Sharia) from me.\" Get it from me. Allah has made clear the way for women. If a virgin boy commits adultery with a virgin girl, his punishment is 100 lashes and one year exile. And if a married man commits adultery with a married woman, his punishment is one hundred lashes and stoning.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1036","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that a Muslim man came to the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque. You turned away from him. He came to you from the other side and said: O Messenger of Allah! I have committed adultery. He then turned his face towards the Anwar until the man repeated his words four times. So (in this way) when he testified against himself four times, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him to him and asked: \"Are you mad?\" He said: No. He then said: \"Are you married?\" He said: Yes. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \"Take him and stone him.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1037","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that when Ma'az bin Malik (RA) came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he asked him: \"Perhaps you have kissed or teased or cast an evil eye.\" He said: \"No, O Messenger of Allah!\" (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1038","On the authority of Hazrat Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, he said in his address: Allah, the Exalted, appointed Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as His Messenger and revealed the Book to him. In what Allah revealed to you, there was also the verse of stoning. We (ourselves) read it and memorized it and understood it (well). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned him and we also stoned him after him. I fear that after some time someone will say that we do not find any mention of stoning in the Book of Allah. In this way, those people will go astray by abandoning a duty that Allah revealed, although the punishment of stoning is established in the Book of Allah for every married man and woman when there is evidence or pregnancy or confession (of adultery and adultery). (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1039","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"When the slave girl of one of you is guilty of adultery and her adultery becomes apparent, then he should restrain her and not reprimand her.\" If he commits adultery again, he should limit it and not reprimand him. If he commits adultery for the third time and his adultery is revealed, then sell him, even if it is for a rope made of hair.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) and these words are from Muslim."
"1040","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Set limits on your slaves and concubines.”"
"1041","It is narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain that a woman from Jahina tribe came to the Prophet and she was pregnant by adultery. He said: O Prophet of Allah! I deserve a limit, so impose a limit on me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called her guardian and advised him: \"Be kind to her and when she gives birth, bring her to me.\" So he did so. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered about her (the woman), so her clothes were tied tightly. Then he gave an order about her and she was stoned to death. Then he offered her funeral prayer, Hazrat Umar said: O Prophet of Allah! You offer her funeral prayer even though she was guilty of adultery? He said: \"He has repented in such a way that if he were to be distributed among seventy people of Madinah, he would surround them all.\" Have you found someone better than him who has laid down his life for the sake of Allah?” (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1042","It was narrated from Hazrat Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) stoned a man from the tribe of Islam and stoned a Jewish man and a woman. (It was narrated by Muslim. And the incident of the stoning of a Jewish man and a woman is narrated in Sahihin on the authority of Ibn Umar.)"
"1043","It was narrated from Hazrat Saeed bin Saad bin Ubadah that there used to be a small crippled man in our neighborhood. He committed adultery with one of our slave girls. Hazrat Sa'd (RA) mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH), so he said: \"Put a limit on it.\" Then he said: \"O Messenger of Allah! He is much weaker and weaker than that. He said: \"Take a large branch of a palm tree with a hundred branches, then strike it at the man once.\" So they did so. (It was narrated by Ahmad al-Nasa’i and Ibn Majah and its chain of transmission is good, but there is a difference in its transmission and transmission.)"
"1044","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever you find guilty of the actions of the people of Lut, kill both the perpetrator and the victim.\" And whoever you find misbehaving with a cow, kill both the man and the cow."
"1045","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (RA) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed (an unmarried adulteress) and exiled her. And Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) was also killed and exiled. And Hazrat Umar also killed and exiled. (It was narrated by Tirmidhi and its narrators are reliable, but there is a difference of opinion regarding whether it was suspended or abrogated.)"
"1046","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed men who impersonate women and cursed women who impersonate men."
"1047","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “As far as there is room for protection from imposing a limit, remove the limit.” (It was narrated by Ibn Majah and its chain of transmission is weak.) And it was narrated by Tirmidhi and Al-Hakim on the authority of Hazrat Aisha, Radiyallahu Anhu, with these words: “Remove the limits from the Muslims as far as you can.” (This is also weak.) What has been narrated on the authority of Radiyallahu Anhu? And that is Hazrat Ali's own saying, whose words are: Remove the limits due to doubts."
"1048","On the authority of Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Beware of those dirty deeds which Allah has forbidden.\" And whoever suffers from them, he should remain hidden in the veil placed by Allah and he should repent to the Lord of Allah (in secret), because whoever reveals his case to us, we will enforce the command of Allah and leave him.”"
"1049","It is narrated from Hazrat Aisha (RA) that when my acquittal was revealed in the Holy Qur'an, the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) stood on the pulpit and mentioned it and recited the Qur'an. When he came down from the pulpit, he decided on two men and one woman and they were restricted. (Narrated by Ahmad and Al-Charu and referred to by Bukhari.)"
"1050","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the first incident of blasphemy in Islam was by Sharik bin Sahma. He was accused by Hilal bin Umayyah of adultery with his wife. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: \"Bring evidence, otherwise you will be punished.\" (Then) the narrator narrated the entire hadith. (This hadith has been narrated by Abu Al-Ala and its narrator is Thaqa. And in Bukhari, a similar hadith has been narrated on the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him.)"
"1051","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi'ah, I have found the covenant of Hazrat Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and those after them. I did not see them punishing slaves with more than forty lashes. (Narrated by Malik and narrated by Al-Thawri in his Jama`ah.)"
"1052","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever slanders his slave (or concubine), he will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, unless it is as he has said, that is, (that slander is true.”) (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1053","Narrated by Hazrat Aisha, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"A thief's hand should be cut off for stealing a quarter of a dinar or more.\" (Bukhari and Muslim - these words are from Muslim). And Bukhari's words are: \"A thief's hand will be cut off for a quarter of a dinar or more.\""
"1054","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off his hand while stealing a shield worth three dirhams. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1055","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Huraira that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"May the curse of Allah be upon the thief who steals an egg and cuts off his own hand.\" And he steals the rope and cuts off his own hand.” (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1056","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do you recommend one of the limits set by Allah?” Then he stood up and delivered the sermon and said: “People! Verily, this is what killed the people before you: when an honorable man among them stole, they would let him go, and when a weak (low status) man stole, they would impose a limit on him.” (Bukhari and Muslim. And these words are from Muslim)."
"1057","Hazrat Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is no punishment of dismemberment for the one who cheats and robs.”"
"1058","It was narrated from Hazrat Rafi' bin Khadij (RA) that I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"There is no punishment for cutting off the hand while gleaning fruit and date-palm trees.\""
"1059","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Umayyah Makhzoomi (RA) that a thief was brought to the Messenger of Allah (PBUH). He confessed to the theft, but the goods were not found with him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: \"I do not think that you have stolen.\" He said: Why not! (I stole.) You repeat the same two or three times. Then he gave the order and his hand was cut off. After that, he was brought to his service, and he said: \"Ask Allah's forgiveness for your sin and repent to Him.\" He said: I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him, then he said three times: \"O Allah! Accept his repentance.'' In it is the saying of the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace: \"Take him and cut off his hand, then mark him.\""
"1060","On the authority of Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When a limit is established on a thief, then no ransom (fine) will be imposed on him.\""
"1061","Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated from the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was asked about the dates hanging on the trees, and he said: \"There is no blame on a needy person if he eats them there and does not fill his feet.\" And whoever leaves there with something, there is a ransom and a punishment. And whoever takes some of the dates after they reach the threshing floor and it is equal to the value of the shield, then the penalty of disobedience will be imposed on him."
"1062","It was narrated from Hazrat Safwan bin Umayyah that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: While he had ordered to cut off the hand of the man who had stolen his (Safwan's) cloak and he had interceded for him: \"Why did you not do this before bringing him to me (to forgive him?\")"
"1063","It is narrated from Hazrat Jabir (RA) that a thief was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) and he said: \"Kill him.\" The people said: \"O Messenger of Allah! He has stolen.\" He said: \"Cut off his hand.\" So his hand was cut off. Then he was presented again, so he said: \"Kill him.\" Hazrat Jabir (RA) mentioned it as before. Then it was brought for the third time, then mentioned in the same way. Then he was arrested and presented for the fourth time in the same way. Then he was arrested and presented for the fifth time, so he said: \"Kill him.\""
"1064","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik (RA) that a man was brought to the Prophet (PBUH) who had drunk alcohol. You gave him about forty (40) lashes with two sticks. It is narrated by Anas (RA) that Hazrat Abu Bakr (RA) also gave this punishment. When Hazrat Umar (RA) came to the Caliphate, he consulted the Companions (RA). Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Auf (RA) said that the lightest punishment is eighty (80) lashes, so Hazrat Umar (RA) ordered the same. Every one of me is a saint and this is dearer to me. And in this hadith it is also said that a man testified against Waleed that he saw Waleed vomiting alcohol. On this Hazrat Uthman (RA) said: He had drunk and vomited."
"1065","Hazrat Mu'awiya (RA) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) said about a drunkard: \"When he drinks alcohol, flog him.\" Then when he drinks alcohol again, whip him again. Then when he drinks the wine for the third time, then whip him again. Then when he drinks alcohol for the fourth time, blow his neck.”"
"1066","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Huraira, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When someone among you strikes, he should refrain from (striking) the face.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1067","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There should be no boundaries in the mosques.\" (Narrated by Tirmidhi and Al-Hakim)."
"1068","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (RA) that when Allah revealed the sanctity of alcohol, only alcohol made from dates was drunk in Madinah at that time. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1069","It is narrated from Hazrat Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the prohibition of alcohol was revealed, at that time it was prepared from five things: grapes, dates, honey, wheat and barley. And khamar (alcohol) is everything that covers the intellect. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1070","Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Every intoxicating substance is wine and every intoxicating substance is forbidden.” (Muslim)"
"1071","On the authority of Hazrat Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whatever is intoxicating in large quantities, even a small quantity of it is forbidden.\""
"1072","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Abbas (RA) that for the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) the Nabeez of Munqi was prepared in Mushkiza. You used to drink it on that day, on the second day and on the third day as well. Then, when it was the evening of the third day, he would drink it himself, make others drink, and if there was anything left, he would throw it away. (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1073","Hazrat Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah the Exalted has not placed healing for you in that which He has forbidden to you.” (Narrated by Bayhaqi and authenticated by Ibn Hibban)."
"1074","It is narrated from Hazrat Wail Hazrami that Tariq bin Suwayd (RA) asked the Prophet (PBUH) about wine that he used to make it for medicine. He said: \"It is not a medicine but a disease.\" (Narrated by Muslim, Abu Dawud and other imams)."
"1075","It was narrated from Hazrat Abu Barda Ansari that he heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"No crime other than Allah's will should be punished with more than ten lashes.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1076","Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Do not suffer from the mistakes of the Companions of the Most High, except that there are Shariah limits.”"
"1077","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: There is no such person that I would set a limit on him, and if he dies, I would feel sorry for him, except a drunkard. So if he dies, I will pay his dowry. (Narrated by Bukhari.)"
"1078","It is narrated from Hazrat Saeed bin Zayd, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever is killed while protecting his property is a martyr.\""
"1079","It is narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Khabab that I heard my father narrating: He used to say that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: (After me) temptations will occur. O servant of Allah! So in these (times of temptations) do not become a victim and do not become a murderer."
"1080","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever dies in such a state that he never fought Jihad and never thought of Jihad in his heart, then he died of hypocrisy.\" (Narrated by Muslim)"
"1081","On the authority of Hazrat Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \"Fight the polytheists with your wealth, your lives, and your tongues.\""
"1082","There is a hadith on the authority of Hazrat Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! Is Jihad also obligatory on women? He said: \"Yes! Jihad is (but) not fighting. It is Hajj and Umrah.” (Narrated by Ibn Majah and its original is in Bukhari.)"
"1083","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Amr that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet and asked for permission to participate in Jihad. He said: \"Are your parents alive?\" He said: Yes! He said: \"Then strive in the service of both of them.\" (Bukhari and Muslim) Ahmad and Abu Dawud have a similar narration regarding Hazrat Abu Saeed (RA). It is added that he said: \"Go back and ask them for permission.\""
"1084","It is narrated from Hazrat Jarir Bajli, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"I am free from guilt from every Muslim who resides among the polytheists.\""
"1085","On the authority of Hazrat Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"There is no migration after the conquest of Makkah, but Jihad and intention remain.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1086","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever fights with the intention that the word of Allah may be exalted, then he is (fighting) in the way of Allah.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1087","On the authority of Hazrat Abdullah bin Saadi, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"The emigration will not end as long as the war with the enemies continues.\""
"1088","It is narrated from Hazrat Nafi, may God have mercy on him, that he said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed the Banu Mustaliq at night, and at that time they were unaware and heedless. So you killed their fighters and took their children as prisoners. This was told to me by Hazrat Abdullah bin Umar. (Bukhari and Muslim) And in this hadith it is also said that Hazrat Jawariyyah was imprisoned on the same day."
"1089","Hazrat Sulaiman bin Buraydah narrates from his father that when the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, would appoint a commander of an army or army, he himself would advise him about the piety of Allah and goodness and goodness about his fellow Muslims. After that he used to say: \"With the name of Allah\" fight in His cause. Fight with those who disbelieve and disbelieve in Allah. Do Jihad but do not betray, do not break the promise, do not commit adultery and do not kill children. And when you face a polytheist enemy, offer them a feast of three things. Which of them is yours? Let them accept it. You accept it and keep your hands off them. First invite them to Islam. If they accept what you say, accept it and withhold your hands from them, then invite them to leave their homes and migrate to the Land of the Emigrants (Dar al-Islam). And tell them that if they do so, they will have the same (of booty and fees etc.) as the (first) emigrants, and the same rulings will apply to them as apply to the emigrants. If they refuse to migrate, tell them that they will be like Bedouin Muslims. The same order of Allah will be imposed on them as is imposed on the common believers and they will not get anything from the booty and wealth except that they participate in Jihad together with the Muslims. If they refuse (to accept Islam), demand Jizya from them. If they accept this from you, then you accept this from them and keep your hands off them. If they refuse (even to pay Jizya), seek help from Allah and start fighting them. And when you besiege the people of a fort and they demand of you that you give them a pledge of peace from Allah and His Prophet, do not do so, but give them a pledge of peace from yourselves and your companions, because breaking the covenant between you and your companions is much milder and lighter than breaking the covenant of Allah and His Messenger. And when you besiege the people of a fort and they demand of you that you surrender to the judgment of Allah, do not do so, but surrender to your judgment, for you do not know whether you will reach the judgment of Allah regarding them or not. (Narrated by Muslim. )."
"1090","It is narrated from Hazrat Ka'b bin Malik that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to go on a campaign, he used to make Turia from another trip. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1091","It is narrated on the authority of Hazrat Muaqal that Hazrat Nu'man bin Muqrin (RA) said, \"I have participated in battles with the Prophet (PBUH). If you did not start fighting at the beginning of the day, then you would delay fighting until the sun went down, favorable winds blew and help came. (Narrated by Ahmad and all three and Al-Hakim called it Sahih and its original is in Bukhari.)"
"1092","It was narrated from Hazrat Saab bin Jathamah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the children and women of the polytheists. He said: \"They are also among them.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)."
"1093","It was narrated from Hazrat Aisha that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to that (polytheist) person who joined him on the day of Badr: \"Go back. I will never take help from a polytheist.\" (Reported by Muslim)"
"1094","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Prophet saw a woman being killed in a battle, so he disapproved of the killing of women and children. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1095","It is narrated from Hazrat Samrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Kill the old (experienced and skilled people) of the polytheists and leave the young ones (minor children) alone.\""
"1096","It is narrated from Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he gave an invitation to battle (to the disbelievers) on the day of Badr. (It was narrated by Bukhari and Abu Dawud narrated this hadith in detail.)"
"1097","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) that this verse was revealed in favor of the Ansar: ) And do not throw yourself into death with your own hands. He even got in between them. (It was narrated by all three. And Tirmidhi, Ibn Hibban and Al-Hakim declared it Sahih.)"
"1098","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, set fire to the palm trees of Banu Nazir and cut them down. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1099","On the authority of Hazrat Ubada bin Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Do not cheat in booty, because cheating in booty is the fire (of Hell) and causes shame for those who cheat in this world and the Hereafter.\""
"1100","It was narrated from Hazrat Awf bin Malik (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) ruled in favor of the killer (Ghazi) regarding the looted property. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud and its original is in Muslim.)"
"1101","It was narrated from Hazrat Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) about the killing of Abu Jahl that they both took their swords and advanced towards Abu Jahl until they killed him. After that he came to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and informed him (of the killing of Abu Jahl). He inquired: \"Which of you killed him?\" Have you cleaned your own swords?” Both said: No. Abd al-Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) says that he then saw the swords of both of them and said: \"Both of you have killed him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided the equipment of Abu Jahl in favor of Mu'adh bin Amr bin Jamuh. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1102","It is narrated from Hazrat Makhool that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set a catapult on the people of Taif. (It has been narrated by Abu Dawud in his Murasil and its narrator is Thaqa. And Aqili has reported it with a weak chain of transmission from Hazrat Ali.)"
"1103","It is narrated from Hazrat Anas (RA) that when the Prophet (PBUH) entered Makkah, he was on his head at that time. When you removed it from your head, a man came to you. He said that Ibn Khatl was clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba. He said: \"Kill him.\" (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1104","On the authority of Hazrat Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed three men by tying them on the day of Badr."
"1105","It was narrated from Hazrat Imran bin Hussain that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave one polytheist man as ransom for two Muslim men. (Narrated by Tirmidhi and declared authentic. And its original is in Muslim.)"
"1106","On the authority of Hazrat Sakhr bin Aila, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"When people accept Islam, they save their blood and their wealth.\""
"1107","It was narrated from Hazrat Jubayr bin Mut’am (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said about the captives of Badr: “If Mut’am bin ‘Adi had been alive, then he would have interceded with me regarding these stinkers, I would have released them for his sake.” (Narrated by Bukhari)"
"1108","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Saeed Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that on the day of Awtas, some captive women were taken into our hands, whose husbands were still alive. Muslims considered intercourse with them to be embarrassing, so on this occasion, Allah Almighty revealed this verse: \"Wal-Muhsnat min-an-Nisa'i illa-ma-malkat-i-manukum\" (Married women are forbidden to you, except those who are your concubines.) (Narrated by Muslim)."
"1109","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent a procession to Najd, and I was also present in it. The Mujahideen who took part in Syria captured many camels as booty. Twelve camels came to each of them. Then they were given an extra camel each. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1110","It was narrated from Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided two parts for the horse and one part for the foot on the day of Khaibar. (The words Bukhari and Muslim are Bukhari's.) In the tradition of Abu Dawud, he prescribed three parts for a man and his horse. Two parts his horse and one part his own."
"1111","On the authority of Hazrat Maan bin Yazid, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: \"Nafl (excess portion) is only after Khums.\""
"1112","It was narrated from Hazrat Habib bin Muslimah (may Allah be pleased with him) that I entered the service of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave a fourth part as Nafl for attacking at the beginning of a journey and a third part for attacking at the time of his return (from Ghazwa). (It was narrated by Abu Dawud, as well as Ibn Jarood, Ibn Hibban, and al-Hakim called it Sahih.)"
"1113","It was narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give something more to some Jihadi forces, especially in addition to the share of booty. It was not included in the normal army division. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1114","It is narrated from Hazrat Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that if we got hold of honey and grapes during the raids, we would eat them and drink them and not carry them away. (It was narrated by Bukhari.) And it is in the tradition of Abu Dawud that Khums was not collected from them. (Ibn Hibban called it Sahih.)"
"1115","It was narrated from Hazrat Abdullah bin Abi Ufa (may Allah be pleased with him) that on the day of Khaibar we got some grain, so a man would come and get from it according to his need and then go back. (Narrated by Abu Dawud, and Ibn Jarood and al-Hakim declared it authentic.)"
"1116","On the authority of Hazrat Ruifa bin Thabit (RA), the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, should not ride on the (common) booty of the Muslims in such a way that when he weakens it, he returns it to the booty. And he should not wear any cloth from the (common) booty of the Muslims in such a way that when he wears it out and wears it, he returns it to the booty."
"1117","Hadhrat Abu Ubaidah bin Jarrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I heard the Messenger of Allah (may God bless him and grant him peace) say: “Any one of the Muslims is authorized to give aman (refuge) on his behalf.” It is in the hadith of Hazrat Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that: “The refuge of all Muslims is the same. Even the lowest of them can give shelter.\" Ibn Majah quoted this addition from another chain of transmission: \"Even a person far away from them can give shelter.\" And in the Sahihin, it is narrated by Umm Hani, may Allah be pleased with her: (The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace), said:"
"1118","It was narrated from Hazrat Umar (RA) that he heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \"I will take the Jews and Christians out of the Arabian Peninsula and kill them.\" Even (in Arabia) I will not leave anyone except a Muslim.” (Narrated by Muslim.)"
"1119","It was narrated from Hazrat Umar that the properties of Banu Nazir were among the properties that Allah gave to His Messenger without a fight. On which the Muslims did not run horses or camels. These properties were especially for the Prophet. You used to take out of this wealth the expenses of your wives for the whole year and what was left would be spent on providing horses and weapons for the preparation of Jihad for the sake of Allah. (Bukhari and Muslim)"
"1120","It is narrated from Hazrat Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Battle of Khyber. In this, some goats came into our hands, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided some of them among us and added the rest to the booty. (It was narrated by Abu Dawud. And its narrators are such that there is no problem in them.)"
"1121","On the authority of Hazrat Abu Rafi', may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Indeed, I do not break my covenant, nor do I imprison messengers and ambassadors.\""
"1122","It is narrated from Hazrat Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whatever town you come to and stay in it, you have a share in it.\" And whoever disobeys Allah and His Messenger, his khums belongs to Allah and His Messenger, then it (the remainder of the settlement) is for you.” (Narrated by Muslim)."
